test.method:
Public Kalshi data only, about 1,380 unauthenticated GETs, no orders. Sources ranked: trade tape (second-level prints with taker side) and exchange 1-minute candles (close bid/ask of every team book, carried forward); no replay.
(1) Settled-market list: 6,000 KXCS2MAP markets, Sep 6-Oct 15, for volume per market and per day.
(2) Batched 1-minute candles for EVERY CS2 match that had map markets, Sep 9-Oct 15: 1,383 matches, chosen by schedule with no volume filter, window from 2 h before the scheduled start to 4 h after. Covers the match book and the map-1 and map-2 books (map 3 is not listed). Team A's effective book is the better of A's own book and the complement of B's. For every minute: the incumbent's spread at the previous minute's close and the contracts printed.
(3) The fair the idea's bot would quote around:
- per-map p from the best-of-3 identity M = p^2(3-2p) on the match mid;
- before the scheduled start, F = inverse of that identity on the current match mid, pulled if the match moved more than 5c in 5 min;
- in play, map 1: q = (M - p^2)/(2p(1-p));
- map 2: q = p while map 1 plays, then (M-p)/(1-p) or M/p once map 1's result is known;
- p is fixed at schedule minus 5 min, so nothing looks ahead.
Calibrated at fixed moments (schedule minus 5 min for map 1, map-1 close plus 3 min for map 2) against results. Fit Sep 9-30, holdout Oct 1-15.
(4) Full public trade tapes of both team books for every played map of every 10th match in schedule order: 504 tickers, 237 played maps, 5.0M contracts printed. Quote simulation:
- a resting quote at F +/- h, with h = 5, 7.5 or 10c;
- filled by any print at or beyond our price, up to 50 contracts per print, with nobody queued ahead of us (generous to us);
- maker fee 0 (fee_type quadratic);
- P&L against the map's settled result, clustered by match.
Three variants: ONLY (filled only when the incumbent is wider than us, which is the idea as written), ALL (quote all the time), PRE (before map start only). The match price is bracketed two ways: 'stale' uses the previous minute's close (a live bot would be faster); 'ahead' uses the same minute's close (up to 60 s of look-ahead, which flatters us).
(5) Dota 2: the same candle structure on 110 matches, Oct 3-15 (volume structure only).
Scripts and outputs are in C:/kals-repo/.sweep/hunt-2026-10-15/test-20261015-R1-C3-11/ (analyse2.py, sim3.py, sim3dbg.py, sim3.out, analyse2_cs2.out, analyse2_dota.out, RESULT.json).

