- even E_low (own-market prints only, the kindest estimator) <= $0;
- the sweeper present in >= 80% of observable hours;
- credit-if-paid < $3.00;
- no RATEH programs listed on 2 consecutive weekdays.
Otherwise EXTEND to 10 weekdays with no rule change.

What the sample can detect: at 50 hours, the share of hours with a sweeper (0.42 now) is known to +-0.11 (90%). The per-strike-hour net has an SE of about $1.0-1.4, so +$2 vs 0 is visible and +$2 vs +$4 is not.

